# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. In production these are set for you
# by the Vercel + Supabase Marketplace integration — see SUPABASE_SETUP.md.
#
# With BOTH values present the app switches to Supabase: sign-in appears and
# student work is saved to the database. With either missing it runs entirely in
# the browser's localStorage, with no sign-in and no network. That fallback is
# intentional and is what CI builds against, so leaving this file uncopied is a
# supported way to work.
#
# Supabase → Project Settings → API. The **anon public** key is the right one:
# it is designed to ship in the browser and is safe here because every table is
# protected by row-level security. Never put the service-role key in this file —
# it bypasses RLS entirely.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-KEY

# The canonical public origin — REQUIRED in production alongside the two above.
# Drives canonical URLs, OpenGraph tags and the sitemap; without it they fall back
# to localhost, so social previews and indexing break on the live site.
# (Auth redirects do NOT read this — they use the browser's own origin — so a wrong
# value here degrades SEO rather than breaking sign-in.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com

# Which sign-in methods the UI offers. Defaults to `google` — Google SSO only,
# which is the shipped setup, so you normally leave this unset. Google is the
# default because it needs no email delivery at all: no SMTP, no confirmation
# step, no rate limit.
#
# Widen it only after enabling the matching provider in Supabase → Authentication
# → Providers; an offered button that isn't wired up fails opaquely the instant a
# student clicks it. `magic` and `password` additionally need custom SMTP before
# real users — see the last section of SUPABASE_SETUP.md.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_METHODS=google,magic
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_METHODS=google,github,magic,password

# Only used when Supabase is NOT configured, to unlock the instructor studio in
# local/offline mode. There is NO default: if you leave this unset the studio
# stays locked and its nav link is hidden. It is a client-side convenience, not
# a security control — anyone can read it in the bundle — so set it to something
# non-obvious. Real instructor access comes from the `profiles.is_instructor`
# flag once Supabase is on.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_INSTRUCTOR_PASSCODE=choose-a-non-obvious-passcode
